**Exercise 8 (S).** Decide which of the following sets are subspaces (with proof or counterexample).

(a) $U_1 = \{ x \in \mathbb{R}^3 \mid x_1 + x_2 = x_3 \} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3$;

(b) $U_2 = \{ x \in \mathbb{R}^3 \mid x_1x_2 = 0 \} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3$;

(c) $U_3 = \{ f \in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{R}} \mid f(1) = 2f(0) \} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{R}}$;

(d) $U_4 = \{ f \in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{R}} \mid f(t) \ge 0 \text{ for all } t \in \mathbb{R} \} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{R}}$

**Definition 4.2.1.** A subset $U$ of a $K$-vector space $V$ is a *(linear) subspace* if

(U1) $0 \in U$;

(U2) $u, u' \in U \Rightarrow u + u' \in U$;

(U3) $\lambda \in K, u \in U \Rightarrow \lambda u \in U$.

A subspace is itself a vector space with the restricted operations (note that $-u = (-1)u \in U$). By Lemma 3.1.2, the solution set $L(A, 0)$ of a homogeneous system is a subspace of $K^n$, whereas $L(A, b)$ is not if $b \neq 0$ (since $0 \notin L(A, b)$).
